@chapter AGI Frontend Language
@cindex AGI frontend language

This chapter describes the AGI frontend language as implemented in the EightBol compiler.
The AGI (Adventure Game Interpreter) frontend provides a high-level language for creating
classic adventure games, supporting game logic, room management, and player interaction.
The language is defined by its lexer (@file{agi-lexer.lisp}) and parser (@file{agi-parser.lisp}).
Only the constructs defined in these files are part of the language; any other AGI-like
constructs are not supported by this frontend.

